[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"936","stub":{"id":"936","section":"A) Burned Dam CG to Bond Falls Flowage (6.4-11.5 miles)","altname":"","river":"Ontonagon, M.Br.","difficulty":"ItoIIstandoutIII","states":["USA-MCH"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"low-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"191","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112013","location":{"latitude":"46.3132019042969","longitude":"-89.0538024902344"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117290","location":{"latitude":"46.4057006835938","longitude":"-89.1309967041016"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"11","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"879155","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879588","description":"First drop of Mex-i-min-e Falls.","caption":"Mex-i-min-e Falls","poi_name":"Mex-i-min-e Falls","subject":"","author":"Scott Puthoff","poi_id":"104086","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879155","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879155"}},{"id":"879156","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879589","description":"Here's Tom running off the lip of the second drop above the munchy hole.  We found it was best to hit this one to the right to avoid the meat of the hole.","caption":"Tom running the top of the Falls","poi_name":"Mex-i-min-e Falls","subject":"Tom Sterling","author":"Scott Puthoff","poi_id":"104086","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879156","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879156"}},{"id":"879158","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879591","description":"You definitely want to run this one a little right of center of the hole to avoid being totally submerged, although, this did allow me to loose some momentum to get left and run the rest of the drop.","caption":"Getting munched by the hole","poi_name":"Mex-i-min-e Falls","subject":"Scott Puthoff","author":"Tom Sterling","poi_id":"104086","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879158","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879158"}},{"id":"879157","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879590","description":"After the first two drops, you want to run back to river left on the left side of a rock right in the middle of the flow.  Worst comes to worst, you beach on the rock and scrape over it to finish on the left side of the run.","caption":"Tom lining up for the rest of the Falls","poi_name":"Mex-i-min-e Falls","subject":"Tom Sterling","author":"Scott Puthoff","poi_id":"104086","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879157","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879157"}},{"id":"879159","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879592","description":"I don't think this was a stern squirt as much as the boat just popping back up after hitting the hole.  Still, it's a sweet pic!","caption":"Stern squirt in a creeker - oh no!","poi_name":"Mex-i-min-e Falls","subject":"Scott Puthoff","author":"Tom Sterling","poi_id":"104091","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879159","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879159"}}],"detail":{"id":"936","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Put-in is at Burned Dam Campground either above or below **Mex-i-min-e Falls**, a class III or IV rapid depending upon flow. It may be noted that one of the holes in this drop has been known to forcibly extricate paddlers from their boat. Experienced boaters may be most likely to just park-and-huck this drop.\n\nThe reach from there is a pleasant float with intermittent rockbed rapids. **Little Falls** is marked on the maps where the river enters the Bond Falls Flowage. It is quite possible that the falls itself is buried beneath the waters of the flowage as there is only a short class II drop there now. There is an egress paddle over the waters of the flowage to a public access point off Bond Falls Rd. **Bond Falls** is located below the dam on the north side of the road and is well worth a visit if in the area. Like Agate Falls downstream, it is a high drop onto rock and not runnable but very scenic.\n\nAs the final miles of river before the flowage are primarily moving water, paddlers may wish to use an alternate take-out at Interior Road.","averageGradient":"9","maxGradient":"21","length":"11.2","correlations":[{"reachID":"936","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":"Likely low-boatable. (We need your input. Add a comment or report.)","mediumRunnableRangeComment":"Likely moderate flows. (We need your input. Add a comment or report.)","highRunnableRangeComment":"Probably high flows. (Uncertain. We need your input! Add a comment or report.)","aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"150","beginMediumRunnable":"300","beginHighRunnable":"600","endHighRunnable":"1000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"MIDDLE BRANCH ONTONAGON RIVER NEAR PAULDING, MI","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"04033000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"191","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"4.91","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"46.3568916","longitude":"-89.0765285"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/04033000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/04033000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":"Gauge (164  sq.mi. drainage) lies midway down this reach, thus very accurately reflects actual flow.","status":{"status":"low-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"191","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["112013","117290"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-89.05421579528802,46.31306992528226],[-89.05429537220994,46.31331912811248],[-89.05439390554312,46.313639128112015],[-89.05482210554248,46.314073594777994],[-89.05495250554226,46.31530759477607],[-89.05514970554196,46.315787594775315],[-89.05551190554138,46.3162677281079],[-89.05570917220774,46.3167705947738],[-89.05547810554145,46.31702179477344],[-89.05392710554383,46.317706594772346],[-89.05336577221141,46.31820892810492],[-89.05346370554457,46.31891752810378],[-89.05376017221079,46.31930612810322],[-89.0545509055429,46.320014928102125],[-89.05524230554181,46.3209751281006],[-89.05537357220828,46.3215465280997],[-89.05514197220862,46.32211772809882],[-89.05467937220938,46.322780194764505],[-89.0547119055426,46.3231685947639],[-89.055766305541,46.32415179476237],[-89.05606270554053,46.32449479476185],[-89.05596297220734,46.3250889280942],[-89.055137705542,46.325751194759846],[-89.05517037220858,46.32597979475952],[-89.05619237220702,46.32639172809223],[-89.05751070553828,46.3274207947573],[-89.05780657220447,46.32822079475602],[-89.05787210553774,46.32867779475532],[-89.05806990553742,46.328883594754984],[-89.05869657220313,46.32886112808837],[-89.05909270553582,46.32863279475538],[-89.06047950553369,46.32744519475722],[-89.06084237219977,46.3273997947573],[-89.06117217219929,46.327491394757146],[-89.06140297219889,46.32762859475696],[-89.06140257219892,46.3279941947564],[-89.06041150553382,46.3292277280878],[-89.06050990553365,46.32966199475379],[-89.06103710553282,46.33027919475285],[-89.06126750553244,46.33080492808534],[-89